  "title": "Dua of Noon (Zuhr)",
  "data": "Perform the Noon Prayer at the beginning of its time; but first, when it is midday (zuhr), recite this doxology (zikr):\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَةً وَّلَا وَلَدًا وَّلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُ شَرِيْكٌ فِي الْمُلْكِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُ وَلِيٌّ مِّنَ الذُّلِّ وَكَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا۔\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI WA LAAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAHU WAL HAMDU LILLAAHIL LAZEE LAM YATTAKHIZ SAAHIBATAW WA LAA WALADAW WA LAM YAKUL LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL MULKI WA LAM YAKUL LAHU WALIYYUM MINAZ ZULLI WA KABBIRHU TAKBEERAA.\nGlory be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and praise be to Allah, Who has taken no consort and no son, has no partner in dominion, and needs no protector out of weakness; so magnify Him with the greatest magnification.\nIf you have not yet performed the ritual ablution, hurry to do so and observe the [Etiquettes of the Noon (Zuhr) Prayer](I21).",
  "merits": "It is reported that Imam al-Baqir (a) instructed Muhammad ibn Muslim to keep on saying this doxology just as he keeps his eyes from harm."
}
